    "stem": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "During aerobic respiration, cells respire substrates such as glucose to produce ATP.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 6
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Some events that occur during aerobic respiration are:",
        "source": {
          "qp": 6
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          "The respiratory substrate breaks down into smaller and smaller molecules. These series of reactions are described as catabolism.",
          "Coenzymes take part in various reactions. In some reactions, coenzymes are reduced or oxidised.",
          "Carbon dioxide is released."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "parts": [
      {
        "key": "a",
        "label": "(a)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 6,
          "ms": 8
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Aerobic respiration occurs in four successive stages: glycolysis (<b>G</b>), link reaction (<b>LR</b>), Krebs cycle (<b>KC</b>) and oxidative phosphorylation (<b>OP</b>).",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Complete Table 3.1 to show which events occur in each stage of aerobic respiration. Use a tick (<i>✓</i>) to show that the event does occur or a cross (✗) to show that the event does <b>not</b> occur.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
